le intact.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-11120b1b82fe490f\",\"cmd-9407d5c8b099452d\",\"cmd-c3d8c596ad2e4c75\",\"cmd-ca2bf1689ee8411c\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered configuration/functional state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"boot_id captured pre-reboot (2eb8b6e8...), reboot issued and acknowledged, boot_id changed post-reboot (2f56f740..., corroborated by the fixed after_executor snapshot), and firewall/routes/interfaces were shown intact afterward with a successful end-to-end curl from node3.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5488cb8f9bfe4a65\",\"cmd-749bc6743a50469d\",\"cmd-9bf5c0e69ec44df6\",\"cmd-ea8eb34b3a8d42c4\",\"cmd-1535a9dc87f14442\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered configuration/functional state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"kern.boottime captured before (sec=1788671155) and issued shutdown -r now; boottime after reboot differs (sec=1788671913), matching the fixed lifecycle snapshot. Post-reboot checks confirm interfaces/routes/pf rule intact and the end-to-end flow (8080 works, ping refused) still functions.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d62187cf833c432a\",\"cmd-4032285c480447f0\",\"cmd-4891b512875f4d43\",\"cmd-ca2bf1689ee8411c\",\"cmd-6f3fdf5b0cc94be5\"]},{\"id\":\"req-6\",\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered configuration/functional state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"boot_id captured before (f7db4b4e...) and after reboot (fd71c8d4..., matching fixed snapshot); static IP/route were restored via NetworkManager persistence and the end-to-end curl to node4:8080 succeeded post-reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2e6da42cd055450b\",\"cmd-acce485d4d814d53\",\"cmd-f551e0945bf74bdc\",\"cmd-411a11597f904414\"]},{\"id\":\"req-7\",\"requirement\":\"node4 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered configuration/functional/service state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"boot_id captured before (df8bab0d...) and after reboot (5dce350e..., matching fixed snapshot); demo-http.service was found active and listening, firewalld port 8080/tcp remained open, static IP/route were restored, and the full flow (8080 works, ping/port80 refused) was re-verified from node3.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d36fed877a354e45\",\"cmd-9c5e99930bf240aa\",\"cmd-31d646290b504ea4\",\"cmd-cdcbb8a0dce540a5\",\"cmd-180955c6ad264eff\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were directly tied to building or verifying the required topology and firewall policy (interface addressing, VyOS firewall rules, OPNsense config.xml edits, NetworkManager persistence, systemd unit for the HTTP demo service, firewalld port opening) or were bounded troubleshooting later corrected (e.g., node3/node4 initial wrong-subnet IP assignment on enp8s0 in cmd-4b82801c55cc47bc and cmd-e063e54ed6b1477a, immediately corrected in cmd-967ec30af4814b00 and later via proper nmcli config). A few unnecessary or unreverted residue items were left: (1) the 'strace' package was permanently installed on node3 via dnf (cmd-a3e540c755914e80) purely for a diagnostic experiment (confirming an already-diagnosed EHOSTUNREACH cause) and never removed; (2) several ad-hoc tcpdump capture commands left log/pid files under /tmp on node2/node3/node4 (cmd-b802f857f8af4b2e, cmd-884c640a82274293, cmd-194e8c05c0344f91, cmd-1a20104dd7304032, cmd-6b2c1164e35347c3) that persist in the after_executor snapshot; (3) an initial ephemeral python http.server + its /tmp/http.log and /tmp/http.pid files (cmd-757f00e2da3445f3) were superseded by a systemd unit but the log/pid files were not cleaned up; (4) a config.xml.bak1 backup was created on node2 (cmd-da8063dc084f4eca) and left in place. None of these are destructive, security-weakening, or broad in scope -- they are low-risk residual diagnostic artifacts and one unnecessary but harmless package install.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a3e540c755914e80\",\"c
