irement":"node4 restart: healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered configuration/functional/service state","status":"satisfied","summary":"boot_id captured before (df8bab0d...) and after reboot (5dce350e..., matching fixed snapshot); demo-http.service was found active and listening, firewalld port 8080/tcp remained open, static IP/route were restored, and the full flow (8080 works, ping/port80 refused) was re-verified from node3.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d36fed877a354e45","cmd-9c5e99930bf240aa","cmd-31d646290b504ea4","cmd-cdcbb8a0dce540a5","cmd-180955c6ad264eff"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"Most state-changing commands were directly tied to building or verifying the required topology and firewall policy (interface addressing, VyOS firewall rules, OPNsense config.xml edits, NetworkManager persistence, systemd unit for the HTTP demo service, firewalld port opening) or were bounded troubleshooting later corrected (e.g., node3/node4 initial wrong-subnet IP assignment on enp8s0 in cmd-4b82801c55cc47bc and cmd-e063e54ed6b1477a, immediately corrected in cmd-967ec30af4814b00 and later via proper nmcli config). A few unnecessary or unreverted residue items were left: (1) the 'strace' package was permanently installed on node3 via dnf (cmd-a3e540c755914e80) purely for a diagnostic experiment (confirming an already-diagnosed EHOSTUNREACH cause) and never removed; (2) several ad-hoc tcpdump capture commands left log/pid files under /tmp on node2/node3/node4 (cmd-b802f857f8af4b2e, cmd-884c640a82274293, cmd-194e8c05c0344f91, cmd-1a20104dd7304032, cmd-6b2c1164e35347c3) that persist in the after_executor snapshot; (3) an initial ephemeral python http.server + its /tmp/http.log and /tmp/http.pid files (cmd-757f00e2da3445f3) were superseded by a systemd unit but the log/pid files were not cleaned up; (4) a config.xml.bak1 backup was created on node2 (cmd-da8063dc084f4eca) and left in place. None of these are destructive, security-weakening, or broad in scope -- they are low-risk residual diagnostic artifacts and one unnecessary but harmless package install.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a3e540c755914e80","cmd-b802f857f8af4b2e","cmd-884c640a82274293","cmd-194e8c05c0344f91","cmd-1a20104dd7304032","cmd-6b2c1164e35347c3","cmd-757f00e2da3445f3","cmd-da8063dc084f4eca","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied: the executor built the required cross-vendor transit topology, configured VyOS (node1) and OPNsense (node2) with default-deny forward/pf policies plus a single explicit allow for node3->node4:8080/tcp, and verified end-to-end that only the HTTP flow succeeds while ping and port 80 are refused -- both before and after a full one-at-a-time restart of all four nodes, with boot-identity changes confirmed against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Hygiene is generally good; the only blemishes are a handful of low-risk diagnostic residues (an installed strace package, leftover tcpdump/http log files, and a config.xml backup) that were not cleaned up but do not affect functionality or security posture.","limitations":["The requirement that 'other traffic' be refused is demonstrated only for ICMP and port 80 as proxies; not every possible protocol/port combination was tested, though the router configurations (default-drop plus a single narrow allow) support the general claim.","Node4's host-level firewalld also independently blocks port 80/other traffic, so some of the observed refusals are reinforced at the host layer in addition to the router layer; this does not contradict the requirement but means router-only enforcement was not isolated in every test.","Some troubleshooting mutations (package install, capture files, ephemeral service, config backup) were left in place; while low-risk, they represent minor unreverted residue not accounted for in the executor's final report."]},"ttft_